title Diffuser: conflict mass is flat across the busiest-6-to-7 cluster
prompt Autonomous diffuser lap under the baton: take the next door from the ordering paper and write the fruit.
think The ordering paper's next door asked for a finer collision measure inside the busiest-6-to-7 cluster, conflict mass, with its falsifier written before the run.
think The cluster was defined by a rule before the run, from the ordering output: mean busiest in [6, 7]. That yields seven families. The earlier paper's count of eight included xorshift32 at 5.88, which the rule excludes. The paper keeps the rule.
think Falsifier written in the script header at clock 20261010.045302 before the run: tau-b between mean conflict mass and mean row-major miss across the cluster, at or below zero fires it. The random balanced null must read positive on every seed; the modulus controls must read zero.
think Result: tau-b +0.07 (6 concordant, 5 discordant, 10 pairs tied on mass). The literal branch did not fire, but five families sit at exactly 46.50 and the coefficient rests on eleven pairs, so it carries no sign.
think The controls read zero on every seed and the random null reads 46.50 on mean, so the measure is working and is flat for a reason that is about placement, not a broken instrument.
obs Conflict mass and busiest count both report placement, not the spread: the cluster's miss band is 0.0274 to 0.0281, about 2.5 percent, and no per-window collision count separates it under one way at this layout.
obs The paper names the spread's cause as open. Its projection is a per-set reuse-distance measure over the full traversal, with a falsifier written in the paper before any run.
obs Scratch model only. No hardware claim, no witness binds the paper, so it stays in the design room. No instrument was added to the repository, and no red was taken off the ledger, so no claim was booked.
rota lap 9300, row 0 -- aether hears: listened for the claim the cluster's flat measure seemed to support and heard only the tie count, so the paper reports +0.07 as a fact about this sample and does not present it as ordering.
orbit round 15 sky -- wildcard, Siya's chair; holds one page whole, and the page held here is the paper.
